# Screenshot → code triage

When the user attaches a **screenshot** of UI to fix — do not open-ended explore. Resolve a file first.

1. Read image for chrome text / route / overlay chips.
2. Overlay id visible → `./scripts/agent-ui-source.sh <id>` → open `file:` / `entry:`.
3. Else label → `agent-ui-source.sh --label "…"` or `docs/agent-ui-map.md`.
4. Else feature obvious → one `AGENTS.md` entry + domain skill.
5. Else on-screen → `agent-ui-route.sh` + one dump **or** `agent-ui-hit.sh` → source.
6. Still ambiguous → `agent-ui-overlay.sh on`, one overlay shot, then off.

Id → file: `docs/agent-ui-sources.json` via `agent-ui-source.sh`. Hit/overlay = lookup only; tap by `ontrack.*` testID. Missing id → add in same change. Full flow: agent-ui skill.
